      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto",
          "value": "<p>In several passages, we find that support of Torah scholars is compared to the support of the house of God, as it is written: But be strong, O Zerubbabel\u2014says the Lord\u2014be strong, O high priest Joshua son of Jehozadak; be strong, all you people of the land\u2014says the Lord\u2014and act! For I am with you\u2014says the Lord of Hosts (Haggai 2:4). [ . . . ]</p>\n<p>Fortunate is the generation that you provide for\u2014because you understand whence scholars and their students are sustained, just as you know the scholars\u2019 straitened circumstances and provide for them, so you will be called a good and faithful provider in the heavens and on earth, as were those who provided for the Jewish people in ancient times. You descend from those early saints, your forefathers and the elders of your region, the scholars of the West, which is a place filled with the divine presence [shekhinah] more than any other, even the Tabernacle and the Temple, the place of the divine presence and the area of prostration. Moreover, wisdom has been found in Spain [Aspamya] from the earliest times until now, for it was explained that in the time of Alexander of Macedon, when he sought to rise up to the heavens, the scholars of the land of Israel in the House [Temple] advised him to go to Spain [Sefarad], for there were found scholars from the first exile. And also, on several occasions,</p>",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
